{
  "name": "fig06-disintegration",
  "description": "Fig 6b — cell disintegration as a grain-swap equivalence. A cell-level coarse-grained metabolism process and a molecular catalyzed-reaction network realize the SAME external interface at two different grains of description: coarse ⇄ fine. Lump the closed catalytic loops of the reaction network and you recover the coarse metabolism process; disintegrate the coarse process and you recover the network. Both grains are shown side by side, each wired to its own store cluster. All DRAFT processes: unit-bearing ports + behavior contracts, no update dynamics.",
